    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1000">

                <pb facs="1347" n="1337" xml:id="pg1337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.0031/3–145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-01T14:00:00+07:00">March 1, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 3—1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>334. ReDeptel 1522, November 23, 5 p.m.;<anchor n="9" xml:id="d1000-f1"/> Embstel
                    1978, December 8, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d1000-f2"/> and Embdes 15,
                    December 18.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d1000-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Foreign Affairs Political Vice Minister<anchor n="12" xml:id="d1000-f4"/> handed
                    to me on February 23 brief oral statement on commercial policy of Chinese
                    Government summarized as follows:</p>
                <p>Chinese Government voluntarily supports free trade policy for which in recent
                    years U. S. Government has energetically sought general acceptance and
                    implementation, both at home and abroad, and earnestly seeks unremitting
                    collaboration. When the Chinese Government establishes a postwar commercial
                    policy it will be based on principles of reciprocity and equality in accordance
                    with concept of international economic collaboration enunciated in Atlantic
                        Charter<anchor n="13" xml:id="d1000-f5"/> as well as in spirit of article 7
                    of Mutual Aid Agreement between Chinese and U. S. Governments.<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d1000-f6"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
